### wasmer login --help
Login into Wasmer

Usage: wasmer login [OPTIONS] [TOKEN]

Arguments:
  [TOKEN]
          The API token to use when communicating with the registry (inferred from the environment by default)
          
          [env: WASMER_TOKEN=sk_smL0rpvWS3m7nyYoUSOwIv1CYsvFb8E1i2kXP3lc0CC57K]

Options:
      --no-browser
          Variable to login without opening a browser

  -v, --verbose...
          Generate verbose output (repeat for more verbosity)

      --wasmer-dir <WASMER_DIR>
          Set Wasmer's home directory
          
          [env: WASMER_DIR=]
          [default: /home/runner/.wasmer]

      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          The directory cached artefacts are saved to
          
          [env: WASMER_CACHE_DIR=]
          [default: /home/runner/.wasmer/cache]

  -q, --quiet
          Do not print progress messages

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          The format to use when generating logs

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable logs
          - json: Machine-readable logs
          
          [env: LOG_FORMAT=]
          [default: text]

      --registry <REGISTRY>
          Change the current registry
          
          [env: WASMER_REGISTRY=]

      --log-events <LOG_EVENTS>
          Which span events to log
          
          [env: LOG_EVENTS=]
          [default: close]
          [possible values: new, close, all]

      --color <COLOR>
          When to display colored output
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

### wasmer --help
wasmer 7.5.0

Usage: wasmer [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  login            Login into Wasmer
  auth             Manage authentication in Wasmer
  publish          Publish a package to a registry [alias: package publish]
  cache            Manage the local Wasmer cache
  validate         Validate a WebAssembly binary
  compile          Compile a WebAssembly binary
  config           Get various configuration information needed to compile programs which use Wasmer
  self-update      Update wasmer to the latest version
  inspect          Inspect a WebAssembly file
  init             Initializes a new wasmer.toml file
  wast             Run spec testsuite
  binfmt           Unregister and/or register wasmer as binfmt interpreter
  whoami           Shows the current logged in user for the current active registry
  add              Add a Wasmer package's bindings to your application
  run              Run a WebAssembly file or Wasmer container
  journal          Manage journals (compacting, inspecting, filtering, ...)
  package          Package related commands
  container        Container related commands. (inspecting, unpacking, ...)
  deploy           Deploy apps to Wasmer Edge [alias: app deploy]
  app              Create and manage Wasmer Edge apps
  cron             Manage cron jobs for Wasmer Edge apps
  ssh              Run commands/packages on Wasmer Edge in an interactive shell session
  namespace        Manage Wasmer namespaces
  domain           Manage DNS records
  gen-completions  Generate autocompletion for different shells
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -V, --version
          Print version info and exit

  -v, --verbose...
          Generate verbose output (repeat for more verbosity)

  -q, --quiet
          Do not print progress messages

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          The format to use when generating logs

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable logs
          - json: Machine-readable logs
          
          [env: LOG_FORMAT=]
          [default: text]

      --log-events <LOG_EVENTS>
          Which span events to log
          
          [env: LOG_EVENTS=]
          [default: close]
          [possible values: new, close, all]

      --color <COLOR>
          When to display colored output
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

### wasmer config --help
Get various configuration information needed to compile programs which use Wasmer

Usage: wasmer config [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  get   `wasmer config get $KEY`
  set   `wasmer config set $KEY $VALUE`
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --wasmer-dir <WASMER_DIR>
          Set Wasmer's home directory
          
          [env: WASMER_DIR=]
          [default: /home/runner/.wasmer]

      --cache-dir <CACHE_DIR>
          The directory cached artefacts are saved to
          
          [env: WASMER_CACHE_DIR=]
          [default: /home/runner/.wasmer/cache]

  -v, --verbose...
          Generate verbose output (repeat for more verbosity)

  -q, --quiet
          Do not print progress messages

      --registry <REGISTRY>
          Change the current registry
          
          [env: WASMER_REGISTRY=]

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          The format to use when generating logs

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable logs
          - json: Machine-readable logs
          
          [env: LOG_FORMAT=]
          [default: text]

      --token <TOKEN>
          The API token to use when communicating with the registry (inferred from the environment by default)
          
          [env: WASMER_TOKEN=sk_smL0rpvWS3m7nyYoUSOwIv1CYsvFb8E1i2kXP3lc0CC57K]

      --log-events <LOG_EVENTS>
          Which span events to log
          
          [env: LOG_EVENTS=]
          [default: close]
          [possible values: new, close, all]

      --prefix
          Print the installation prefix

      --bindir
          Directory containing Wasmer executables

      --color <COLOR>
          When to display colored output
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --includedir
          Directory containing Wasmer headers

      --libdir
          Directory containing Wasmer libraries

      --libs
          Libraries needed to link against Wasmer components

      --cflags
          C compiler flags for files that include Wasmer headers

      --config-path
          Print the path to the wasmer configuration file where all settings are stored

      --pkg-config
          Outputs the necessary details for compiling and linking a program to Wasmer, using the `pkg-config` format

